WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.336
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.739
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.207
Let's get to some news.

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:11.144
Today President Biden gave
his first commencement address

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:15.281
as commander in chief at the
Coast Guard Academy graduation.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.284
Yeah, Biden's speech
lasted about 30 minutes

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.953
until a Coast Guard captain
fired off a rescue flare.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:25.458
It's like, "Wrap it up, buddy."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.994
Even Navy S.E.A.L.s were looking
at the Coast Guard like,

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.429
"How did you make it
through that?"

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.197
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.732
But this was nice. Biden
personally handed out diplomas

00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:36.469
to all 240 graduates.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.405
Then Fox News criticized him for
more government handouts.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:43.209
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.943
You could tell Biden is 78

00:00:44.943 --> 00:00:47.413
'cause he also gave
every graduate a check for $10.

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:48.447
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:52.152
"Don't spend it all
in one place."

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:54.287
At the end of his visit,
Biden received a gift.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.889
It was pretty special.
Take a look at this.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.390
-On behalf of the class of 2021,

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.461
I would like to present to you
this token of our appreciation.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.665
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.436
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.071
-That's a good joke.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.672
He said the same thing
at Christmas

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:15.308
when his grandkids got him
a Life Alert.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:18.411
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.113
On his ride home, he used the
sword to open a string cheese.

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:25.185
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.487
Anyway, that'll explain why
he shows up to his next event

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.955
wearing an eye patch.
You what I'm saying?

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.123
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.558
Got a sword.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.326
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.594
What is he gonna do with this?

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:37.296
Popping bottles of Ensure.

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:41.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.135
Side note, by the way --

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:45.271
why does the Coast Guard
carry swords?

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.605
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:48.107
Shouldn't it be
a harpoon or something?

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.042
[ Laughter ]
Guarding the coast like,

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.778
"Something's coming down
the coast!

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.580
Let's wait till they land
and get about two feet from us,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.116
then we can defend ourselves."

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.984
Get them bazookas.
What are we doing?

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.318
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:00.687
Yeah, Biden spent the day

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.254
with the Coast Guard's
newest graduates,

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.756
which brings us
to a new segment called

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.892
"Inspiring words
from your commander in chief."

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.362
♪♪

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.964
-You're a really dull class.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.967
♪♪

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:18.537
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:21.941
-Hey, this is interesting.
I saw that kids ages 13 to 17

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.176
can officially trade stocks

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:27.080
with Fidelity's
new youth investing accounts.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.015
Yeah, you'll know your kids
are too into trading

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.149
when they're up at 3:00 a.m.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.218
for the Asian markets,
downing Pixy Stix.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.520
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.489
I can already see a dad
threatening to cut off

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.257
his son's allowance
and the son just smiles

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.159
and lights a cigar with a 50.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.894
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.496
"Why don't you go mow the lawn,
Dad?"

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.097
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:48.133
Get this. Google just announced
a new privacy feature

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.802
that will allow users to delete

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.905
the last 15 minutes
of their search history.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:55.875
It's easy. You just go to
Settings and turn on Perv Mode.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.143
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:00.713
That's very simple.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.549
Some more business news --
Dunkin' Donuts just announced

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.018
a new partnership
with a paint company

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:08.554
for the chain's first ever
paint collection.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.756
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.959
It's for anyone who's ever
walked into a Dunkin' Donuts

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.227
like, "I want to live here."

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:18.664
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:20.899
I saw that next month
General Mills is releasing

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:25.304
four of its most popular cereals
in oatmeal form.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.373
Or you could just pour milk
into your favorite cereal

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.375
and wait literally 10 seconds.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.178
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.280
It's Wheaties.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.848
It's spackle.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.617
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.785
That's right,
Lucky Charms oatmeal.

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:41.988
And if you're looking for
a healthier breakfast option,

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.290
I recommend drinking
Dunkin' Donuts paint.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.493
[ Laughter ]
I'm not a doctor.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.528
Finally, I read about
an Air France flight

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:52.598
that travelled nearly seven
hours from Paris to Montreal

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.701
powered by used cooking oil.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.171
Yeah, it's great if you don't
mind spending seven hours

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:01.306
knowing that you're on a plane
powered by used cooking oil.

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:04.210
It's like, "Only 6 hours
and 49 minutes left, everybody.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.279
We're almost -- We can do this.
We can do this."

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.646
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:09.581
Yep, the cooking-oil flight
landed on time,

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:11.717
but they had to wait 10 minutes
under a heat lamp

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.152
until someone came
and picked them up.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.355
Did you see that President Biden
actually test-drove the elec--

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.423
-Yes.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.359
-It was in Michigan yesterday.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:24.363
But they gave him a full tour of
the whole thing, and anyways,

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.432
he had some things to teach them
as well, apparently.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.200
-Really?
-Well, they asked him

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.104
what he thought of
the whole truck.

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:33.273
Here's what he had to say.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.856
[ Laughter and applause ]
What?

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:52.492
-Really?

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:55.460
That's what he said to them?
-I don't know.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.197
Later in his tour
of the plant --

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.532
he was looking at
the whole plant in Michigan,

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.733
and he said this.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.923
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.724
-Wow, what's he talking about?

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:26.926
-He's at the plant.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.128
Might as well talk about
the truck or something.

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.897
Then he left them with this.

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:50.382
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:51.817
-Really?
-I don't know, man.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:53.086
They got him out of there.

